WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
Oops All In combines party mini games with a shared betting system.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:06.000
But how does the pot actually work?

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:11.000
Share the room code and everyone begins with exactly 100 pretend chips.

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:16.000
Before the prompt is revealed, every player must commit 5 chips into the center.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:18.000
Then you see the game and the betting begins.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:20.000
You match, raise, or fold.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:21.000
Got a short stack?

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:25.000
You can still play, but you only win the exact portion you matched.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:27.000
The stakes escalate fast.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:31.000
From round 3, eligible games unlock the option to go all-in.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:34.000
Once bets lock, you actually play the mini game.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:38.000
Answering, drawing, or drafting to claim that pot.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:42.000
Some cooperative or bluffing games, like Same Brain and Who's Faking,

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:45.000
skip betting entirely for a fixed 5-chip entry.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:48.000
That massive central pot pays out to the mini-game winner.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:52.000
The remaining chips are tallied and the board clears for the next hand.

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:54.000
And after you've played through your chosen number of rounds,

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:58.000
the player holding the most pretend chips wins the entire session.
